// Automaton outpost: a precursor station the automatons keep (GDR-0026's site kinds; GDR-0110). It never moves
// (`anchored`: it turns on its cores' gyros, but no ram, shot or plume shoves it) and has no engines. A shielded hub
// without guns (two shield emitters, a fusion reactor, two capacitors, two radiators, two cores) and three spokes,
// each joined to the hub by one bridge block and with an automaton core of its own: a scanner mast in front, a
// cannon on each side spoke, facing the front. Shot off, a spoke keeps its place and turns on its own, like the
// Warden's fists. The hub is the rich salvage. Eight cannons cleared 12 % of rim runs, three 48 %; two clear about
// as often as a hunter den. PLACEHOLDER layout (content batch of 18 Oct 2026, tuned with the
// headless voyage runner, docs/results/encounters-balance-2026-10-18.md).
(
    id: "automaton_outpost",
    name: "Automaton outpost",
    summary: "A 13×9 precursor station: a shielded hub, a scanner mast and two cannon spokes, fixed in place.",
    description: "It cannot chase you, but it turns to bring the [[part:automaton_cannon|cannons]] on its side spokes to bear, and nothing shoves it. Each spoke has its own [[part:automaton_core|core]]: shoot a bridge through and a side spoke fights on alone. The hub has no guns of its own: it keeps its [[part:shield_emitter|shields]] up and holds the richest salvage on the site.",
    lore: "The shipyard's records call it a waystation. Nothing has waited there for a long time.",
    tags: ["enemy", "station"],
